# osTicket Help Desk Implementation

## Project Summary

This project demonstrates the installation and configuration of osTicket on an Ubuntu Server virtual machine using Oracle VirtualBox.

The project uses Apache, PHP, and MariaDB to deploy a functional help desk ticketing system.

### Technologies Used

- Oracle VirtualBox
- Ubuntu Server
- Apache2
- PHP
- MariaDB
- osTicket 1.18.4

---

## Installation and Configuration

### 1. Virtual Machine Setup

Created an Ubuntu Server virtual machine using Oracle VirtualBox.

![VirtualBox](screenshots/01-virtualbox.png)

### 2. Ubuntu Server Installation

Installed Ubuntu Server and configured the network environment.

```bash
sudo apt update
sudo apt upgrade -y
ip addr
```

![Ubuntu](screenshots/02-ubuntu-installation.png)

### 3. Apache Installation

Installed and enabled the Apache web server.

```bash
sudo apt install apache2 -y
sudo systemctl enable --now apache2
sudo systemctl status apache2
```

![Apache](screenshots/03-apache.png)

### 4. PHP Installation

Installed PHP and the required extensions for osTicket.

```bash
sudo apt install php libapache2-mod-php php-mysql php-imap php-xml php-mbstring php-gd php-curl php-intl php-apcu php-zip -y
```

Verified the PHP installation:

```bash
php -v
php -m
```

![PHP](screenshots/04-php.png)

### 5. MariaDB Installation

Installed MariaDB and configured the database for osTicket.

```bash
sudo apt install mariadb-server -y
sudo systemctl enable --now mariadb
```

![MariaDB](screenshots/05-mariadb.png)

### 6. osTicket Installation

Downloaded osTicket 1.18.4, extracted the application files, and configured the web directory.

```bash
sudo chown -R www-data:www-data /var/www/html/osticket
```

Prepared the osTicket configuration file and completed the web-based installation.

![osTicket](screenshots/06-osticket-installation.png)

### 7. Ticket Creation and Testing

Accessed the Support Center, created a test ticket, and verified ticket management through the Staff Panel.

![Test Ticket](screenshots/07-test-ticket.png)

